                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Once you get past the poor optimization and get the game running properly, there’s a really fun action JRPG underneath. Despite being a musou game, it honestly doesn’t feel like one to me—the combat feels much closer to the modern Ys games, while the hubworlds slightly remind me of Twilight Princess.\nThe combat is fast and satisfying, and the character variety, leveling, fun but limited vocation system, and weapon proficiency give the progression plenty to enjoy. The art and characters are great, and the simple, light-hearted story is exactly what you’d expect from Dragon Quest.\n\nOverall, I’d definitely recommend it to action JRPG lovers and Dragon Quest fans.",
